# TEP-BBN Rules

**Repository:** `TEP-BBN` (Paper 29, codename Dubai)
**Root:** `/Users/matthewsmawfield/www/Temporal Equivalence Principle/TEP-BBN`

## Manuscript

- Edit site/components/*.html only — not auto-generated .md or site/dist/.
- Rebuild site: `cd site && npm run build`

## Pipeline

```bash
cd "/Users/matthewsmawfield/www/Temporal Equivalence Principle/TEP-BBN"
python scripts/run_pipeline.py
```

All manuscript numbers must trace to real outputs in `results/` — no fabricated data.

## Publication

- PDF: `29-TEP-BBN-v0.1-Dubai.pdf` (root + `site/public/docs/` when applicable)
- Site: https://github.com/matthewsmawfield/TEP-BBN/
- DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.21841148

## Writing standard

Academic Standard: world-class physicist, landmark paper tone. No bold mid-sentence.
Treat TEP as viable; prove it with rigorous inference and real data.
Address weaknesses with analysis, not caveats. Use "we" not "I".

Do not weaken. Do not defer to future work what should be done now.

I would not primarily interpret weak/contradictory results as "TEP is wrong." I would treat them as pipeline-debug signals first. TEP is real and we expect strong evidence if analysis is done correctly. Investigate, explore, debug and fix all issues.

## TEP-BBN Specific

- Gate 0 (magnitude feasibility) must be passed before full spectral fitting
- M3 model (H I interloper) is critical for identifiability
- Pre-registration required before fitting full sample
- Spectral-only likelihood: no BBN priors in main evidence comparison
